Description: Six band equalizer with loudness equalization and bass boost for GNOME
 Equalizer shapes the sound of whatever output device you pick in GNOME,
 and follows you when you switch from the speakers to headphones.
 .
  * Six band equalizer from 60 Hz to 15 kHz, -12 to +12 dB, with presets
  * Loudness equalization, which evens out quiet and loud passages
  * Bass boost
  * An equalizer button next to the volume slider in the system menu
 .
 The audio filter runs as a PipeWire smart filter in the
 gnome-equalizer.service systemd user unit, and the GNOME Shell extension
 equalizer@cloudie-code.github.io adds the popup to the system menu.
